# Pipeline conventions

## Canonical entrypoints

| Task | Script |
|------|--------|
| Full hourly pull + load | `pipeline/orchestrators/orchestrate_hourly_full.py` |
| Full daily pull + load | `pipeline/orchestrators/orchestrate_daily_full.py` |
| Watcher one-cycle | `pipeline/orchestrators/orchestrate_watcher_cycle.py` |
| Hourly pull | `pipeline/pull/hourly/pull_all.py` |
| Daily pull | `pipeline/pull/daily/pull_all.py` |
| Hourly load | `pipeline/load/hourly/load_all.py` |
| Daily load | `pipeline/load/daily/load_all.py` |

## Path taxonomy

`pipeline/paths.py` defines raw CSV layout under `raw/{vendor}/{cells,groups}/{rat}/{hourly,daily}/`.

## Legacy scripts

`scripts/pipeline/` and `scripts/pull_all_raw*.py` remain for compatibility. New work goes in `pipeline/`.

## Huawei daily staging

Daily exports land in `raw/huawei/{cells,groups}/all/daily`, then split by RAT before `pipeline/load/daily/load_all.py`.

## Shared core

- `core/pipeline_run.py`, `core/pipeline_load.py`, `core/pipeline_ingest_verify.py`
- `core/raw_pm_files.py`, `core/pm_retention.py`

`raw/` and `*.db` are runtime data — never treat as source to edit.
